# Force LF line endings on text fixture files so byte-level
# comparison tests pass identically on Windows and Linux. Without
# this, Windows git's autocrlf converts committed LF to CRLF at
# checkout, and the fixture-comparison tests (ParseSuccessReportTests,
# any future committed-golden tests) fail because the generator emits
# LF and the test compares against the CRLF-converted file on disk.
#
# Scoped to text fixture file types only. Native Windows artifacts
# (*.csproj, *.ps1, *.cmd, etc.) keep their default behavior.
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.bas    text eol=lf
*.yaml   text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf

# C# source: LF everywhere. C# raw string literals (`"""..."""`)
# preserve source-file line endings rather than normalizing to LF
# (per the C# 11 design decision). Tests that compare raw-string
# inputs against the expected `"...\n"` shape fail on Windows
# checkouts where autocrlf converts committed LF to CRLF. Pinning
# *.cs to LF makes those tests deterministic across platforms.
# Confirmed against VbaModuleBodyLoaderTests on 2026-05-18.
*.cs     text eol=lf
